 "fix": "src/renderer/aces2.hpp hue_atan2 and src/renderer/aces2_gamut.cpp Transform::forward; the same in web/colour/colour.wgsl. Both paths changed together.",
 "reference_moved": "the fixed C++ reference against the old one over the criterion 2 grid: at most 4.1e-5 (srgb-extended), 2.6e-6 (rec2100-pq), 6.6e-6 (SDR). Colour difference: Delta E ITP at most 0.0013 (HDR); CIEDE2000 at most 0.0004 (SDR).",
 "ocio": "Not rerun: OpenColorIO is not installed on this machine and installing it is a download. Delta E ITP is a Euclidean distance, so the new reference is within 0.0391 + 0.0013 = 0.0404 of OCIO for rec2100-pq and 0.0067 + 0.0013 = 0.0080 for srgb-extended (bound 1.0 max, 0.25 p99). CIEDE2000 is not a metric in the strict sense, so for SDR the same sum (0.0028 against 0.5) is an estimate. A direct rerun of tools/colour/ocio_compare.py is still owed.",
 "does_not_prove": "That every GPU's sin, cos and atan2 sit within the WGSL limits; mode 3 draws errors at random within them, which is not a worst case for each input. It shows that the CPU reference reproduces the failure at those limits and that the fixed pipeline does not."
}
